# Test: a forked plugin contributes a firewall table it reserved, through the
#       firewall engine operation, and the table is in the ruleset listing.
# Spec: spec-container-3-network, Wiring Test row 4, phases 1 and 3
# VALIDATES: tablesReplaceHandler
#   (internal/component/firewall/register_contribution.go), reached over RPC
#   from the forked fakeowner plugin through sdk.Plugin.FirewallTablesReplace;
#   refuseUnreservedContribution (contribution.go) accepts ze_fakeowner, which
#   the plugin reserved from its init(), and replaceContributedTables registers
#   it under the plugin's name and reconciles it through ApplyAll.
# PREVENTS: a producer that can run forked writing through a process-local
#   registry call, which changes only its own copy.
# Why not a unit test: only a forked process proves the request crosses RPC
#   under its authenticated name, and only the applied ruleset shows the table.
#
# The config holds a firewall section. ApplyAll loads the OS default backend
# on demand, so the table would reach the kernel without it, but the firewall
# engine runs only for a present firewall root, and its orderly stop is what
# removes every ze table (FlushAllTables), the contributed one included.
#
# Red before phase 3: the handler refused every contribution as not built, so
# the barrier never saw table-accepted.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT
tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
firewall {
	backend nft
}
plugin {
	external fakeowner {
		run "ze plugin fakeowner"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

# Barrier: the contribution was accepted.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture daemon/await-answer table-accepted "show fakeowner outcome":exit=0

# The applied ruleset holds the contributed table. The operator names it
# without the ze_ prefix its kernel name carries.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze cli -c "show firewall ruleset fakeowner":exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=fakeowner
